window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>A doctor, a witch goddess, and the Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse walk into a bar…</p> <p>Meet Erin Kelly. You can call her Doc.</p> <p>Yes, she’s a doctor. A cardiothoracic surgeon from Boston, to be precise.</p> <p>She’s also the cursed descendant of an ancient witch goddess who’s destined to stop the Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse from monkey-stomping humanity into a primordial puddle.</p> <p>How Doc’s supposed to do that exactly is a bit of a mystery—especially to her.</p> <p>No worries, though. She’ll figure it out. Right after she tracks down her aforementioned arcane ancestor. There’s just one small wrinkle—she’s not been seen in a thousand years. Maybe two.</p> <p>Regardless, Doc and her impromptu coven of witches, prophets, angels, snarky hellhounds, and the occasional giant or two better hurry. The Horsemen are on the hunt. And the end times are nigh.</p> <p>Good thing Purgatory’s nice this time of year, huh?</p> <p>Tick-tock, tick-tock…</p> <p>STEVE GILMORE is a graduate of West Point with an overactive imagination and an affinity for snarky anti-heroes. His urban fantasy novels are a distinctive blend of military grit, supernatural legend, and apocryphal lore that have been enjoyed by fans around the world. The Purgatory Knights series is recommended for listeners who enjoy T. R. Cameron’s Witch Warrior Series, Martha Carr’s The Warrior Series, Auburn Tempest’s Case Files of an Urban Druid, and Jim Butcher’s The Dresden Files.</p> <p>Are you a Heaven’s Dark Soldiers fan? Although a stand-alone series, Purgatory Knights takes place in the HDS universe and is set between the events of Wrath of the Fallen and Rage of the Heavens.</p>"; 
